.TH CRONEN 1 2026-10-24 cronen "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cronen \- see what pacman \-Syu is about to do before you run it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cronen
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-check " | " \-\-json " [" \-\-waybar ]]
.br
.B cronen
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cronen
is a terminal UI for Arch Linux that shows pending repo and AUR updates,
the Arch news you haven't read, anything that needs manual intervention,
and risky packages (kernel, GPU drivers, glibc, systemd), with links to
upstream and the packaging changelog.
When you're happy, it hands the terminal to
.B sudo pacman \-Syu
or your AUR helper.
.PP
cronen only reads.
It never runs
.BR "pacman \-Sy" ,
so it can't cause a partial upgrade: pending updates come from
.BR checkupdates (8),
which syncs a temporary copy of the database.
.PP
An update is flagged when unread news mentions it or its pkgbase, when an
unread post requires manual intervention, when it matches the watchlist,
when its major version changes, when Python's minor version changes (AUR
packages depending on it likely need rebuilding), or when it is a kernel
(reboot afterwards).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print a short plain-text summary, most important first, and exit with a
status from
.B EXIT STATUS
below.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a one-line JSON summary, for example
.br
.nf
{"updates":18,"aur":2,"flagged":11,"critical":1,"unread_news":2,"pacnew":1,"reboot":true}
.fi
.I updates
counts repo and AUR updates together,
.I critical
counts unread news requiring manual intervention, and an
.I errors
array lists any source that failed.
.TP
.B \-\-waybar
With
.BR \-\-json ,
print
.IR text ,
.IR tooltip ,
.I class
and
.I alt
for a waybar custom module.
The class is one of
.BR none ,
.BR updates ,
.BR attention ,
.B critical
or
.BR error .
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use bundled sample data and touch nothing on the system: no config, state
or cache is read or written, and upgrading runs nothing.
Also works with
.B \-\-check
and
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP 14
.BR j / k ", " \(da / \(ua
Move.
.TP
.BR g / G
Top / bottom.
.TP
.BR ctrl+d / ctrl+u
Half a page down / up in the detail or news pane.
.TP
.B tab
Switch focus between panes.
.TP
.B /
Filter the package list;
.B enter
keeps the filter,
.B esc
clears it.
.TP
.B n
News screen.
.TP
.B m
Mark the selected news item read (on the updates screen: the news behind
the selected package's flags).
.TP
.B o
Open the upstream URL (on the news screen: the post) with
.BR xdg\-open (1).
.TP
.B c
Open the packaging changelog.
.TP
.B r
Refresh everything, bypassing the cache.
.TP
.B U
Upgrade: confirm with
.BR y ,
then cronen suspends and runs the upgrade command.
Afterwards it reloads everything and shows the number of
.I .pacnew
files and whether to reboot.
Only a successful upgrade (exit status 0) marks the news up to now as read.
.TP
.B ?
Help.
.TP
.BR q ", " ctrl+c
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is TOML.
A missing file is fine, every key is optional, and cronen never writes to
it.
.TP
.BR aur " (default " true )
Check the AUR for updates of foreign packages.
.TP
.BR aur_helper " (default " """""" )
.B paru
or
.B yay
to upgrade with
.B paru \-Syu
or
.B yay \-Syu
instead of
.BR "sudo pacman \-Syu" .
.TP
.B upgrade_command
A command line that overrides the above, split on whitespace.
.TP
.B watchlist
Package globs to always flag.
The defaults are
.IR linux* ,
.IR nvidia* ,
.IR mesa ,
.IR vulkan\-* ,
.IR glibc ,
.IR systemd ,
.IR grub ,
.IR pacman ,
.IR openssl ,
.I python
and
.IR gcc* .
.TP
.BR watchlist_mode " (default " extend )
.B extend
adds
.B watchlist
to the defaults;
.B replace
uses it alone.
.TP
.BR news_days " (default " 30 )
When the last upgrade is unknown, news from this many days counts as
unread.
.TP
.B ignore_major
Globs, matched against name and pkgbase, whose major version bumps aren't
flagged.
.TP
.BR show_debug " (default " false )
List makepkg
.I <name>\-debug
splits.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
aur_helper = "paru"
watchlist = ["zfs*"]
ignore_major = ["firefox"]
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
For
.BR \-\-check :
.TP 5
.B 0
Nothing to do.
.TP
.B 10
Updates available.
.TP
.B 20
Attention needed: at least one update is flagged.
.TP
.B 30
An unread news item requires manual intervention.
.TP
.B 1
Error: a source (checkupdates, the AUR, the news feed) failed.
With a source missing, cronen can't tell
.I nothing to do
from
.IR "didn't look" .
An unreadable
.I pacman.log
is not an error.
.PP
.B \-\-json
exits 0 once it has printed.
Invalid flags exit 2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cronen/config.toml
Config, default
.IR ~/.config/cronen/config.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cronen/state.json
Read news and the last upgrade cronen ran, default
.IR ~/.local/state/cronen/state.json .
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cronen/
The news feed and AUR responses, kept for 15 minutes, default
.IR ~/.cache/cronen/ .
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
Read for the time of the last full system upgrade.
If it is unreadable, the last upgrade is unknown and news from the last
.B news_days
days counts as unread.
.SH EXAMPLES
A waybar module:
.PP
.RS
.nf
"custom/cronen": {
    "exec": "cronen \-\-json \-\-waybar",
    "return\-type": "json",
    "interval": 1800,
    "on\-click": "foot \-e cronen"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
checkupdates syncs a temporary database from your mirror on every run, so
don't poll often.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR checkupdates (8),
.BR pacdiff (8),
.BR paru (8),
.BR yay (8)
.PP
https://github.com/leNITHISH/cronen
